NEW3=[
S('fs','Storage','Create an Azure File Share','Create an SMB file share and mount it on a VM.',1,6,'Storage accounts>Select account>Data storage>File shares>+ File share','Enter <b>Name</b> and choose the access <b>Tier</b>.|Set quota if needed, then <b>Review + create</b>.|Open the share → <b>Connect</b> and copy the Windows or Linux mount script.|Run the script on the VM.','Drive or mount point shows the share contents.','Unmount, then delete the share.','Mount fails => outbound port 445 blocked by firewall or ISP.|Access denied => check identity-based or key authentication.','storage/files/storage-how-to-create-file-share',[('CLI','az storage share-rm create --storage-account stappdev001 --name share1 --quota 100','Creates a 100 GiB share. Needs Contributor on the account.')]),
S('lc','Storage','Configure Lifecycle Management','Move or delete blobs automatically by age to save cost.',2,6,'Storage accounts>Select account>Data management>Lifecycle management>Add a rule','Enter a <b>Rule name</b> and choose the rule scope and blob type.|On <b>Base blobs</b>, set conditions (last modified more than N days ago) and actions: move to cool, move to archive, delete.|Add filters (prefix) if needed, then <b>Add</b>.','Rule is listed Enabled; blob tiers change after the daily run.','Disable or delete the rule.','Nothing moved => rules run about once a day; allow 24 hours.|Wrong tier => check last-access versus last-modified condition.','storage/blobs/lifecycle-management-policy-configure','','','Test on a prefix first; archive blobs have rehydration delay and early-deletion fees.'),
S('sas','Storage','Generate a Shared Access Signature (SAS)','Give time-limited, scoped access without sharing account keys.',2,6,'Storage accounts>Select account>Security + networking>Shared access signature','Select allowed services, resource types and permissions.|Set <b>Start and expiry</b> time, allowed IP addresses and HTTPS only.|Select the signing key and <b>Generate SAS and connection string</b>.|For least privilege use a container or blob <b>Generate SAS</b> with a user delegation key instead.','Open the SAS URL; expired or out-of-scope requests fail.','Rotate the signing key or revoke a stored access policy.','403 AuthenticationFailed => clock, expiry or signature mismatch.|Blocked => IP restriction or firewall.','storage/common/storage-sas-overview','','Prefer user delegation SAS signed with Entra credentials.|Keep expiry short.','Use stored access policies for revocation.'),
S('keys','Storage','View and Rotate Storage Access Keys','Manage the two account keys used for shared-key access.',2,6,'Storage accounts>Select account>Security + networking>Access keys','Select <b>Show</b> to reveal a key or connection string.|Update apps to use key 2.|Select <b>Rotate key</b> on key 1, then repeat for key 2 on a schedule.','Apps keep working after rotation.','Disable key access via the account setting Allow storage account key access.','App fails after rotation => it still used the old key.','storage/common/storage-account-keys-manage','','Store keys in Key Vault; prefer Entra ID authentication.','Set a key expiration policy.'),
S('stfw','Storage','Configure the Storage Firewall','Limit network access to selected VNets and IP ranges.',2,6,'Storage accounts>Select account>Security + networking>Networking>Firewalls and virtual networks','Set public network access to <b>Enabled from selected virtual networks and IP addresses</b>.|Add the VNet and subnet (needs a service endpoint) or IP ranges.|Tick the exception for trusted Azure services if required.|Select <b>Save</b>.','Allowed clients connect; others get 403.','Set access back to all networks (not recommended) or add the missing rule.','403 from your PC => add your public IP.|Backup or logging fails => enable trusted services exception.','storage/common/storage-network-security','','Prefer private endpoints for sensitive data.','Document allowed ranges.'),
S('vmss','Compute','Create a Virtual Machine Scale Set','Run identical VMs that scale in and out automatically.',3,7,'Virtual machine scale sets>Create','<b>Basics</b>: group, name, region, zones, Orchestration mode Flexible, image, size, authentication.|<b>Networking</b>: VNet, subnet, load balancer.|<b>Scaling</b>: set initial instances and a custom autoscale policy (min, max, scale-out on CPU).|<b>Management</b> and <b>Health</b>: enable monitoring and health extension.|<b>Review + create</b>.','Instances show Running; autoscale rule is listed.','Delete the scale set and its load balancer.','Scale-out blocked => vCPU quota.|Unhealthy instances => app health probe.','virtual-machine-scale-sets/flexible-virtual-machine-scale-sets-portal','','Spread across zones; patch with rolling upgrades.','Use images and extensions, not manual changes.'),
S('asvc','Compute','Create an App Service Web App','Host a web app without managing servers.',1,7,'App Services>Create>Web App','<b>Basics</b>: group, unique name, Publish (Code or Container), Runtime stack, OS, region, App Service plan and pricing plan.|<b>Deployment</b>: connect GitHub if wanted.|<b>Networking</b> and <b>Monitor + secure</b>: enable Application Insights.|<b>Review + create</b>.|Deploy via <b>Deployment Center</b>.','Browse to name.azurewebsites.net.','Delete the app; delete the plan if unused.','503 => app crash; check Log stream.|Name taken => names are global.','app-service/overview','','Turn on HTTPS only; use managed identity for secrets.','Use staging slots and autoscale; Basic plan is not for production.'),
S('func','Compute','Create a Function App','Run event-driven code on a serverless plan.',2,7,'Function App>Create','Choose the <b>hosting option</b> (e.g. Flex Consumption or Consumption).|<b>Basics</b>: group, name, runtime stack and version, region.|Set storage, networking and Application Insights.|<b>Review + create</b>.|Add a function under <b>Functions</b> → <b>Create</b>.','Function appears; test it from Code + Test.','Delete the function app and its storage account if unused.','Function not triggering => check trigger bindings and storage connection.|Cold start => use a plan with pre-warmed instances.','azure-functions/functions-create-function-app-portal'),
S('aci','Compute','Create a Container Instance','Run a container quickly without orchestration.',1,7,'Container instances>Create','<b>Basics</b>: group, name, region, image source and image, size.|<b>Networking</b>: Public or Private, DNS label, ports.|<b>Advanced</b>: restart policy and environment variables.|<b>Review + create</b>.','Container state Running; browse the FQDN.','Delete the container group.','Image pull error => registry credentials or name.|Port unreachable => port not exposed in both group and image.','container-instances/container-instances-quickstart-portal',[('CLI','az container create -g rg-app-dev-001 -n aci-demo --image mcr.microsoft.com/azuredocs/aci-helloworld --dns-name-label aci-demo-001 --ports 80','Creates a public container. Result shows an FQDN.')]),
S('aks','Compute','Create an AKS Cluster','Run Kubernetes with a managed control plane.',3,7,'Kubernetes services>Create>Kubernetes cluster','<b>Basics</b>: group, cluster name, region, zones, pricing tier, version, authentication (Microsoft Entra ID with Azure RBAC recommended).|<b>Node pools</b>: node size and count.|<b>Networking</b>: choose network plugin and policy.|<b>Integrations</b>: Container registry, Monitor, Defender.|<b>Review + create</b>.|Connect with the commands below.','kubectl get nodes shows Ready nodes.','Delete the cluster; the node resource group is removed.','Nodes NotReady => check subnet IP space and quota.|Image pull fails => attach the ACR.','aks/learn/quick-kubernetes-deploy-portal',[('CLI','az aks get-credentials -g rg-app-dev-001 -n aks-app-dev','Merges credentials into kubeconfig. Needs a cluster user role.'),('CLI','kubectl get nodes','Lists nodes; expect STATUS Ready.')],'Use private clusters and Entra auth.','Separate system and user node pools; plan upgrades.'),
S('ag','Monitoring','Create an Action Group','Define who is notified and what runs when an alert fires.',1,9,'Monitor>Alerts>Action groups>Create','<b>Basics</b>: group, name, display name, region.|<b>Notifications</b>: add Email/SMS/push/voice.|<b>Actions</b>: add Webhook, Logic App, Function or ITSM.|<b>Review + create</b>, then use <b>Test action group</b>.','Test notification received.','Delete the action group (alert rules lose the action).','No email => check spam and rate limits.','azure-monitor/alerts/action-groups'),
S('la','Monitoring','Create a Log Search Alert','Alert on the result of a KQL query.',3,9,'Monitor>Alerts>Create>Alert rule','<b>Scope</b>: select the Log Analytics workspace.|<b>Condition</b>: Custom log search, paste the query.|Set measurement, threshold, frequency and lookback.|<b>Actions</b>: attach an action group. <b>Details</b>: severity and name.|<b>Review + create</b>.','Rule fires when test data meets the condition.','Disable or delete the rule.','Never fires => query returns no rows; test it in Logs.|Delay => ingestion latency.','azure-monitor/alerts/alerts-create-log-alert-rule',[('KQL','Heartbeat\n| where TimeGenerated > ago(10m)\n| summarize count() by Computer','Counts heartbeats; alert when a VM is missing.')]),
S('ai','Monitoring','Create Application Insights','Monitor app requests, failures and dependencies.',2,9,'Application Insights>Create','Choose group, name, region and the Log Analytics workspace (workspace-based).|<b>Review + create</b>.|On <b>Overview</b> copy the <b>Connection string</b>.|Set it in the app as APPLICATIONINSIGHTS_CONNECTION_STRING.','Live metrics and Transaction search show requests.','Delete the resource; logs remain in the workspace.','No data => wrong connection string or app not instrumented.','azure-monitor/app/create-workspace-resource'),
S('wb','Monitoring','Create an Azure Monitor Workbook','Build a shared dashboard from logs and metrics.',2,9,'Monitor>Workbooks>New','Select <b>Add</b> → <b>Add query</b>.|Choose Logs, the workspace, and paste KQL; select <b>Run Query</b>.|Add a title and visualization.|Select <b>Done editing</b>, then <b>Save</b> with name, group and location.','Workbook opens for permitted users.','Workbooks → select → Delete.','Empty result => time range or query scope.','azure-monitor/visualize/workbooks-create-workbook'),
S('bpol','Backup & DR','Create a VM Backup Policy','Define schedule and retention for VM backups.',2,10,'Recovery Services vaults>Select vault>Manage>Backup policies>Add','Choose policy type <b>Azure Virtual Machine</b>.|Enter name, sub type (Standard or Enhanced).|Set backup schedule (frequency, time, time zone) and instant restore retention.|Set daily, weekly, monthly and yearly retention.|Select <b>Create</b>.','Policy lists in the vault; assign it to VMs.','Stop using it, then delete it.','Cannot delete => items are still assigned.','backup/backup-azure-manage-vms','','','Match retention to RPO and compliance.'),
S('rst','Backup & DR','Restore a VM from Backup','Recover a VM or its disks from a recovery point.',2,10,'Recovery Services vaults>Select vault>Protected items>Backup items>Azure Virtual Machine>Select VM>Restore VM','Select a <b>Restore point</b>.|Choose <b>Create new</b> (VM or Restore disks) or <b>Replace existing</b>.|Set resource group, VNet and a staging storage account.|Select <b>Restore</b>; track under <b>Backup jobs</b>.','Restored VM boots and data is intact.','Delete the restored VM and staging resources.','Restore fails => staging storage must be in the same region.|Name conflict => choose a new name.','backup/backup-azure-arm-restore-vms'),
S('asr','Backup & DR','Enable Site Recovery Replication (Azure to Azure)','Replicate a VM to another region for disaster recovery.',3,10,'Virtual machines>Select VM>Operations>Disaster recovery','Choose the <b>Target region</b>.|Review advanced settings: target group, VNet, availability and replication policy.|Select <b>Review + Start replication</b>.|Track under the vault → <b>Replicated items</b> until Healthy.','Replication health Healthy; RPO shown.','Replicated items → Disable replication.','Enable fails => VM agent or provider registration.|Vault not found => Azure-to-Azure vault must be in the target region.','site-recovery/azure-to-azure-tutorial-enable-replication','','Use a recovery plan; keep the target network pre-built.','Test regularly; define RPO and RTO.'),
S('tfo','Backup & DR','Run a Test Failover (DR Drill)','Validate DR without affecting production.',3,10,'Recovery Services vaults>Select vault>Replicated items>Select VM>Test failover','Choose the <b>Recovery point</b>.|Pick an isolated test <b>Azure virtual network</b>.|Select <b>OK</b>.|Verify the test VM, then <b>Cleanup test failover</b> and note findings.','Test VM runs in the target region.','Cleanup test failover deletes test resources.','Test VM unreachable => isolated network lacks routes or NSG rules.','site-recovery/azure-to-azure-tutorial-dr-drill'),
S('fo','Backup & DR','Perform a Failover','Switch production to the DR region.',3,10,'Recovery Services vaults>Select vault>Replicated items>Select VM>Failover','Choose the <b>Recovery point</b> (Latest processed or latest).|Tick shut down the machine before failover if possible.|Select <b>OK</b>, monitor the job, then <b>Commit</b>.|Update DNS or traffic routing.','VM runs in the target region and apps respond.','Use failback to return.','Failover job fails => check target network and quota.','site-recovery/azure-to-azure-tutorial-failover-failback','','Run from a documented recovery plan.','Decide who can trigger a failover.'),
S('fb','Backup & DR','Re-protect and Fail Back','Return workloads to the primary region after recovery.',3,10,'Recovery Services vaults>Select vault>Replicated items>Select VM>Re-protect','Select <b>Re-protect</b> to reverse replication.|When healthy, select <b>Failover</b> back to the primary region and <b>Commit</b>.|Re-protect again to restore the original DR direction.','Replication Healthy in the original direction.','Disable replication if no longer needed.','Re-protect fails => original resources must be cleaned up.','site-recovery/azure-to-azure-tutorial-failover-failback'),
S('kvk','Security','Create a Key Vault Key and Certificate','Generate cryptographic keys and certificates in the vault.',2,8,'Key vaults>Select vault>Objects>Keys (or Certificates)>Generate/Import','For a key choose type (RSA) and size, then <b>Create</b>.|For a certificate choose <b>Generate</b>, name, CA type, subject (CN=...), validity and lifetime action.|Select <b>Create</b>.','Object lists Enabled; certificate status Completed.','Delete; soft-deleted items can be recovered.','Forbidden => need Key Vault Crypto Officer or Certificates Officer.','key-vault/certificates/quick-create-cli key-vault/keys/quick-create-cli'),
S('def','Security','Enable Microsoft Defender for Cloud Plans','Turn on threat protection and posture management.',2,8,'Microsoft Defender for Cloud>Management>Environment settings>Select subscription>Defender plans','Switch the plans you need to <b>On</b> (Servers, Storage, Key Vault, Containers).|Select <b>Save</b>.|Review <b>Recommendations</b> and <b>Secure score</b>.','Plans show On; recommendations populate.','Switch plans Off (charges stop).','No data => allow a few hours.|Costs rise => check plan pricing per resource.','defender-for-cloud/enable-enhanced-security','','Assign recommendations to owners; export to Sentinel or SIEM.','Enable on all subscriptions via Policy.'),
S('jit','Security','Enable Just-in-Time VM Access','Close management ports and open them only on request.',3,8,'Microsoft Defender for Cloud>Workload protections>Just-in-time VM access','Open the <b>Not configured</b> tab and select the VM.|Select <b>Enable JIT on 1 VM</b>.|Set ports (22, 3389), protocol, allowed source and max request time; <b>Save</b>.|To connect: select <b>Request access</b> with your IP and duration.','Configured tab lists the VM; NSG shows a temporary allow rule.','Remove the VM from JIT; remove the NSG rules.','Request denied => missing role Microsoft.Security/locations/jitNetworkAccessPolicies/initiate/action.|Option missing => JIT needs Defender for Servers Plan 2.','defender-for-cloud/just-in-time-access-usage'),
S('ddos','Security','Enable DDoS Protection','Protect public endpoints against volumetric attacks.',3,8,'DDoS protection plans>Create','Enter group, name and region; <b>Review + create</b>.|Open the VNet → <b>Settings</b> → <b>DDoS protection</b> → <b>Enable</b> and choose the plan.|Alternative: enable IP Protection on individual public IPs.','VNet shows the plan; metrics appear under the public IP.','Disable on the VNet, then delete the plan.','Cost surprise => plans are billed monthly per plan.','ddos-protection/manage-ddos-protection'),
S('costan','Cost','Analyze Costs with Cost Analysis','Find what drives spend by service, group, tag or resource.',1,11,'Cost Management + Billing>Cost Management>Cost analysis','Select the <b>Scope</b>.|Set the date range and granularity.|Use <b>Group by</b> (Service name, Resource group, Tag).|Add filters; <b>Save</b> the view.','Chart totals match the invoice for the period.','Delete saved views.','Missing tag data => tags apply to new usage only.|Delay => data can lag up to 24 hours.','cost-management-billing/costs/quick-acm-cost-analysis'),
S('adv','Cost','Review Azure Advisor Cost Recommendations','Reduce waste from idle and oversized resources.',1,11,'Advisor>Cost','Filter by subscription.|Open each recommendation (right-size or shut down VMs, reserved instances).|Select <b>Postpone</b> or <b>Dismiss</b> if not applicable, or follow the fix.','Potential savings figure drops after action.','Re-activate a dismissed recommendation if needed.','No recommendations => data takes days; low utilization window.','advisor/advisor-cost-recommendations'),
S('anom','Cost','Create a Cost Anomaly Alert','Get notified of unusual spend.',2,11,'Cost Management + Billing>Cost Management>Cost alerts>Add','Select the alert type <b>Anomaly</b> for the subscription.|Enter name and recipients.|Select <b>Create</b>.','Alert listed under Cost alerts.','Delete the alert rule.','No alert => anomalies need enough usage history.','cost-management-billing/understand/analyze-unexpected-charges')]
